.\"
.\" CLOSE(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH CLOSE 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
close \- close a file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int close(int " fd ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR close ()
closes a file descriptor, so that it no longer refers to any file
and may be reused.
.PP
If
.I fd
is the last file descriptor referring to the underlying open file
description, the resources associated with the open file description
are freed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned.
.PP
On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EBADF
.I fd
is not a valid open file descriptor.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 6 (SYS_CLOSE)
Arguments:      fd (on stack)

    push fd
    push $0
    mov eax, 6
    int $0x80
    add esp, 8
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (2),
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2),
.BR dup2 (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
